+## 10. Decision rules
+
+### ACCEPT
+
+All must hold：
+
+1. experiment `VALID`；
+2. every hard guardrail passes；
+3. inventory >= 1/3；
+4. feature >= 6/9；
+5. overall >= 20/27；
+6. latency/token guardrails pass；
+7. Atomic ambiguity is not used as primary support。
+
+### MIXED
+
+Any of：
+
+- only part of the targeted capability improves；
+- targeted improvement occurs but an efficiency guardrail fails；
+- the conclusion materially depends on Atomic ambiguity；
+- attempt-level evidence is internally inconsistent。
+
+### REJECT / rollback candidate
+
+Any of：
+
+- inventory remains 0/3；
+- bug fixing drops below 9/9；
+- timeout exceeds 3/27；
+- overall drops below 20/27；
+- runtime/infra/trace/grader failure occurs；
+- no targeted improvement and efficiency regresses。
+
+No rollback is automatic。
